 "_comment": "Hours worked and reported satisfaction, by citizenship status NOW (CTZN), for employed holders of a US-earned doctorate living in the United States. Grouped by CURRENT status, unlike the rest of this project, because leverage attaches to the status a person holds now. Visa holders are much younger than citizens here, so READ THE WITHIN-COHORT FIGURES: a pooled comparison largely measures career stage. SELF-REPORTED, and hours are a BANDED category whose TOP BIN IS 'more than 40' -- the public file topcodes it (HRSWKP is the _PUB variable), so 41 hours and 80 hours are the same value. The hours result therefore CANNOT TEST a claim about working far beyond forty, which is where such claims live; it can only say that crossing forty is less common. Both measures are also SELF-REPORTED to a federal survey by people whose right to remain depends on an employer, which is a population with a plain reason to understate. Nothing here identifies visa type or employer.",
 "source": "NSF NCSES, Survey of Doctorate Recipients 2023 public-use file",
